A foundational model is a model that is used to create a model based on the principles of science and/or business logic.  There are many different models that can be used to create a foundational model, including:
- descriptive theories;
- inductive theories;
- psychological theories;
- computer simulation models;
- historical models;
- fixed-model models;
- Bayesian theories;
- theory-based models;
- games;
- modeling devices;
- open- source software;
- reusable models;
- communities;
- and more.
